v7 v2.36.8 - x86-64 assembly LLM/VLM
inference for Windows and Linux
---------------------------------------------
A ~260 KB DLL (v7_threading.dll) and a .so
build from the same NASM sources: quantized
and F32 transformer inference on plain CPU
cores. No Python, no GPU, no dependencies.
Loads from any C program
(LoadLibraryA / dlopen).

Text : Qwen3, Qwen2.5, Llama-3.2, Phi-3-mini,
       SmolLM2, TinyLlama, MiniCPM5
Vision: Qwen3-VL, LLaVA-OneVision, SmolVLM

- AVX2 kernels in NASM: Q8/F32 matmul, fused
  RMSNorm+RoPE, SwiGLU, flash attention,
  AES-NI polynomial sampler
- Work-stealing pool, zero syscalls on the
  spinning hot path
- MicroDB: one LZ4-compressed .db file holds
  weights, tokenizer, config, templates
- SectorLogo64: embedded Logo interpreter on
  every token, with FFI and mid-generation
  stream rewriting (KV rollback + re-prefill)
- RAG on the think stream: retrieval injected
  into the model's own reasoning

web-research agent, 21 validators, 14
benchmarks, database inspection tools.

x64: Windows or Linux, AVX2 CPU (2013+),
4 GB RAM for small models. Docs: docs\
(start with README.md). License: GPL v3.
